  "goodToKnow": "Zeitgenössisch means contemporary, both of the present (zeitgenössische Kunst, Musik, Literatur) and of the same historical period: zeitgenössische Quellen (sources from that time). Der Zeitgenosse is a contemporary, and colloquially just a person: ein seltsamer Zeitgenosse (an odd character). From Zeit (time) and Genosse (companion). Similarly, der Zeitgeist is a German word borrowed into English."
